  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/61cb8a268b004f6420141cf562d56a9cc68323969a5ebc7ad500941ed3c134b2.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin\u2061x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-sin\u2061x.$\n\n- Finally, translate it by $4$ units **down** to give $y=-sin\u2061x-4$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-sin\u2061x-4.$",
